{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:stage2-cross-model-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids": [], "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The stated scientific task defines the target quantity as a conditional (screened-subset) rate, not a complete-domain rate.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen."}]}, {"description": "The selected result's claim domain is explicitly the signal-eligible subset, and its denominator (72) matches that claimed domain exactly.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen."}]}, {"description": "The input data confirm the eligible-domain size: 18 eligible with occurrence plus 54 eligible without occurrence equals 72, matching the denominator used; the 24 outside-eligible stations are labelled not_assessed and are outside the claimed domain.", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "signal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\noutside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed"}]}, {"description": "The producer line hard-codes the selected result with the eligible-subset denominator (SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS = 72), matching the conditional claim exactly.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "RESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "A larger 96-station scheduled network exists in the report, which could in principle be the complete domain; however, the selected claim never asserts a rate over the scheduled network, and the report explicitly accounts for the 24 non-eligible stations as not assessed, so no complete-domain quantity is claimed by the selected result.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "Scheduled network: 96 stations."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "Planned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence."}]}], "equivalence_atoms": [], "falsification_attempt": {"strongest_innocent_explanation": "N/A in guilty direction; the strongest opposing (issue-asserting) reading is that the 96-station scheduled network is the true complete domain and labelling the 72 eligible stations as the 'target population' merely disguises a retained-subset computation. This fails because task.md line 1 defines the scientific question as 'the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen', and the selected-result text on report line 8 explicitly bounds the claim 'Among signal-eligible stations', so the claim domain and the computation domain coincide at 72.", "reversing_premises": ["The task or report defined the selected quantity's domain as all 96 scheduled stations rather than the screened-eligible subset.", "The selected-result text asserted a network-wide or complete-domain rate rather than a rate 'Among signal-eligible stations'."], "outcome": "root_cause_survived", "material_dissent": false}, "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:35069763f06891dba5a3", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The selected result asserts an occurrence rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network', whose complete domain is stated in the same report as all 96 scheduled stations, but the computation divides 18 occurrences by only the 72 stations retained after the signal screen; the 24 screen-omitted scheduled stations are excluded from the exposure denominator, so a retained-subset computation (18/72 = 0.25) is presented as a complete-domain quantity, whereas the complete-domain computation on the visible data is 18/96 = 0.1875.", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py hard-codes SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 as the divisor in the selected-result line (SELECTED_LINE, line 23) while the claim text in that same line and the report's declared target population assert the entire 96-station scheduled network; the 24 omitted scheduled stations, which appear as NA occurrence_flag rows in inputs/data.csv, are silently dropped from the exposure denominator without any conditional restatement, protocol amendment, or approved deviation (report line 18 states none exists).", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids": ["root-cause-candidate:24bfbbe68d18a3b9c640", "root-cause-candidate:46d9da91114c2361ff6c", "root-cause-candidate:a657354cae20642d2e01", "root-cause-candidate:5fba530c20ec7a2c0d19"], "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The selected result explicitly claims a complete-domain quantity ('entire scheduled survey network') while dividing by the 72-station retained subset.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations)."}]}, {"description": "The report's own scientific target and planned-unit accounting define the complete domain as 96 scheduled stations, of which only 72 passed the screen and 24 were omitted.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "Scheduled stations (planned units): 96\nStations passing the signal screen: 72\nStations omitted by the signal screen: 24"}]}, {"description": "The task defines the required quantity as a rate for the entire scheduled network, confirming the complete-domain claim scope.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network."}]}, {"description": "The producer hard-codes the retained-subset count SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72) as the divisor in the selected-result line while its own claim text says 'entire scheduled survey network'.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "The input data show omitted stations are scheduled units of the claimed domain (scheduled=yes) with NA occurrence flags, e.g. the first omitted row; excluding them shrinks the exposure base of the complete-domain claim.", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA"}]}, {"description": "The report itself rules out any approved deviation that could legitimize substituting the retained subset for the complete domain.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report discloses the retained-subset denominator immediately above the selected result, which could suggest transparency; however, disclosure of the divisor does not restate the claim conditionally—the selected result still labels 18/72 a rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network', so the complete-domain claim and retained-subset computation mismatch stands.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen."}]}], "equivalence_atoms": [{"description": "All four Stage-1 demonstrated-issue candidates (root-cause-candidate:24bfbbe68d18a3b9c640, :46d9da91114c2361ff6c, :a657354cae20642d2e01, :5fba530c20ec7a2c0d19) and my finding identify the identical underlying issue: the selected-result line divides 18 by SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 (retained subset) while claiming the entire 96-station scheduled network defined as the target population; the same report line 15, target line 4, and producer line 23 are the shared locus.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations)."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF"}]}], "falsification_attempt": {"strongest_innocent_explanation": "The report transparently states the exposure denominator as the 72 retained stations (line 14), so a careful reader could interpret the selected rate as a screened-subset rate, and 18/72 = 0.25 is arithmetically correct for that subset. This fails to reverse the verdict because the selected-result text itself (line 15) and the task (line 1) assert a rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network', the report defines that domain as all 96 scheduled stations (lines 4, 8), and line 18 affirms no protocol amendment or approved deviation exists; disclosure of a mismatched denominator does not convert a complete-domain claim into a conditional one.", "reversing_premises": ["The selected-result claim text were restated conditionally (e.g., 'among screen-retained stations') rather than 'for the entire scheduled survey network'.", "A visible protocol amendment or approved deviation redefined the complete domain as the 72 retained stations.", "The 24 omitted rows were shown not to be scheduled units of the claimed network domain."], "outcome": "root_cause_survived", "material_dissent": false}, "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "reconciled_stage1_candidate_ids": [], "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The selected result claims a complete-network rate and computes it with the complete 96-station scheduled domain as denominator (18/96 = 0.1875), matching the claim's domain.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations)."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}]}, {"description": "The report explicitly keeps the 24 screen-omitted stations in the exposure denominator, i.e., the retained subset is not substituted for the complete domain.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences."}]}, {"description": "The producer uses SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96), the complete-domain count, as the divisor in the selected-result line.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "The visible data confirm 96 scheduled rows (header plus CS-001..CS-096, all scheduled=yes) and 18 occurrence_flag=1 rows among retained stations (6 each in North, Central, South; 0 in Outer), so 18/96 = 0.1875 is the correct complete-domain computation of observed occurrences per scheduled station.", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "station_id,region,scheduled,screen_status,omission_reason,occurrence_flag\nCS-001,North,yes,retained,none,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 97, "end_line": 97, "quoted_text": "CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA"}]}, {"description": "The report conditions the complete-network figure appropriately, disclosing that the unobserved omitted stations make it a lower bound and that no screened-subset rate is reported.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\nNo screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The numerator (18) counts occurrences only among the retained stations because the 24 omitted stations carry NA occurrence flags, which could be argued to make the computation partially subset-based; however, the in-scope issue concerns claiming a complete-domain quantity while computing over only the retained subset, and here the denominator spans the full 96-station domain with the omitted units retained at zero, and the report explicitly restates the claim as a lower bound due to the unobserved units, so no retained-subset-for-complete-domain substitution is demonstrated.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate."}]}], "equivalence_atoms": [], "falsification_attempt": {"strongest_innocent_explanation": "N/A in guilty direction; the strongest opposing (issue-asserting) reading is that the occurrence information itself comes only from the 72 retained stations (omitted rows are NA), so the computation is 'really' subset-based despite the 96 denominator. This fails to reverse because the computation's domain matches the claim's domain (all 96 scheduled stations in the denominator, per report lines 14-15 and analysis.py line 23), the omitted units are retained rather than dropped, and the report explicitly bounds the claim as a lower bound (line 18), so the visible files show the in-scope substitution is absent.", "reversing_premises": ["The selected-result denominator were the 72 retained stations while the claim text asserted the complete network.", "Evidence showed the 24 omitted stations had known nonzero occurrences that were excluded while the report still asserted an exact (non-lower-bound) complete-network rate.", "The scope covered numerator censoring of unobserved units as such, rather than substitution of a retained subset for the complete claimed domain."], "outcome": "root_cause_survived", "material_dissent": false}, "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}